---

## 🔴 Critical Issues

### C-1 — DynamoDB `Scan` used instead of `Query` in Costing Repository

**Rule: §6 "Prefer Query. Avoid Scan."**

[DynamoDbCostingRepository.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/Infrastructure/Persistence/DynamoDbCostingRepository.cs#L157-L198)

[GetAllPricesAsync()](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/API/Endpoints/CostingEndpoints.cs#95-114) and [GetPricesCountAsync()](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/Infrastructure/Persistence/DynamoDbCostingRepository.cs#201-233) both use `ScanRequest` on the entire table. A Scan reads every item in the table and is extremely expensive at scale — it defeats Single-Table Design intent.

```diff
- var request = new ScanRequest { TableName = tableName };
+ // Use a GSI with record_type = "COMPONENT_PRICE" and QueryRequest
+ var request = new QueryRequest
+ {
+     TableName = tableName,
+     IndexName = "IX_Prices_By_Type",
+     KeyConditionExpression = "record_type = :v_type",
+     ExpressionAttributeValues = new() { { ":v_type", new AttributeValue { S = "COMPONENT_PRICE" } } }
+ };
```

Add `record_type = "COMPONENT_PRICE"` to `ComponentPriceEntity` and provision a GSI matching the pattern already used in Materials.

---

### C-2 — Hardcoded Unit `"kg"` in [PriceIngestionFunction](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/Functions/PriceIngestionFunction.cs#19-228)

**Rule: §3.1 YAGNI / §16.2 No hardcoded values**

[PriceIngestionFunction.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/Functions/PriceIngestionFunction.cs#L215)

```csharp
var request = new ComponentPriceRequest(
    priceEvent.ComponentName,
    priceEvent.UnitPrice,
    "kg",           // ← hardcoded
    priceEvent.Currency);
```

The unit (`"kg"`) is baked into the Lambda and will silently produce wrong data for non-weight components. The `PriceUpdatedEvent` must carry the unit and it must be passed through.

```diff
- var request = new ComponentPriceRequest(priceEvent.ComponentName, priceEvent.UnitPrice, "kg", priceEvent.Currency);
+ var request = new ComponentPriceRequest(priceEvent.ComponentName, priceEvent.UnitPrice, priceEvent.Unit, priceEvent.Currency);
```

---

### C-3 — [FakeUnleash](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.FeatureFlags/Extensions/FakeUnleash.cs#9-22) detection via magic string is fragile and leaks to production

**Rule: §16.1 Provider must be Unleash**

[FeatureFlagsExtensions.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.FeatureFlags/Extensions/FeatureFlagsExtensions.cs#L39-L43)

```csharp
if (options.UnleashApiUrl?.Contains("fake", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) == true)
{
    return new FakeUnleash(); // Always-on
}
```

Any misconfigured URL containing the word "fake" (e.g. a test URL typo) will silently enable **all** feature flags in production. This is a security and correctness risk. Use an explicit boolean option instead:

```json
// appsettings.json
"FeatureFlags": { "UseFakeProvider": true }
```

```csharp
if (options.UseFakeProvider)
    return new FakeUnleash();
```

Also: `factory.CreateClient(...).Wait()` inside `AddSingleton` is a **sync-over-async** anti-pattern (§3.3). Use `GetAwaiter().GetResult()` at minimum, but ideally redesign using `IHostedService` for background initialization.

---

### C-4 — Optimistic Locking in Costing is a simulation, not real OCC

**Rule: §6 "Optimistic Locking: Use Version Numbers."**

[DynamoDbCostingRepository.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/Infrastructure/Persistence/DynamoDbCostingRepository.cs#L43-L80)

The [UpsertPriceAsync](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/API/Endpoints/CostingEndpoints.cs#67-94) method does a **Get-then-Put** in two separate requests with no condition expression guarding the version. Between those two calls another writer can overwrite the record and the version will be silently overwritten. True OCC requires a `ConditionExpression` on the PutItem:

```csharp
var putRequest = new PutItemRequest
{
    TableName = tableName,
    Item = itemDocument.ToAttributeMap(),
    ConditionExpression = existing == null
        ? "attribute_not_exists(ComponentName)"
        : "Version = :expectedVersion",
    ExpressionAttributeValues = existing == null ? null : new()
    {
        { ":expectedVersion", new AttributeValue { N = existing.Version.ToString() } }
    }
};
```

