## 🟠 Major Issues

### M-1 — [Class1.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.FeatureFlags/Class1.cs) leftover file in `PoC.FeatureFlags`

**Rule: §12 Repository Hygiene**

[Class1.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.FeatureFlags/Class1.cs) is a scaffolding artifact with an empty class and should be deleted immediately.

---

### M-2 — `AddProblemDetails()` missing in `PoC.Costing` Program

**Rule: §3.2 "All HTTP APIs must return RFC 7807 ProblemDetails"**

`PoC.Materials` correctly calls `builder.Services.AddProblemDetails()`. `PoC.Costing` does not, meaning built-in exception handlers and `Results.Problem(...)` may lack proper RFC 7807 formatting.

```diff
// PoC.Costing/Program.cs
+ builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();
```

---

### M-3 — Commented-out dead code in [PoC.Populator/Program.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Populator/Program.cs)

**Rule: §12 Cleanup; §3.1 Clean Code**

[Program.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Populator/Program.cs#L22-L30) has 8 commented-out lines of Portuguese startup logging that was apparently used during development. Commented code is noise and must be removed before merging.

---

### M-4 — `JsonSerializerOptions` allocated on every deserialization call (hot path)

**Rule: §3.3 Performance — Minimize heap allocations**

Both ingestion functions create a new `JsonSerializerOptions` instance per message:

```csharp
// MaterialIngestionFunction.cs:123 & PriceIngestionFunction.cs:201
var materialEvent = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<...>(
    messageJson,
    new JsonSerializerOptions { PropertyNameCaseInsensitive = true }); // ← new alloc every call
```

`JsonSerializerOptions` is relatively expensive and is meant to be cached as a static readonly field:

```csharp
private static readonly JsonSerializerOptions JsonOptions = new() { PropertyNameCaseInsensitive = true };
```

---

### M-5 — [GetUniqueComponentsAsync](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Materials/Infrastructure/Persistence/DynamoDbMaterialRepository.cs#137-190) pagination is semantically broken

**Rule: §14.3 Cursor-based Pagination**

[DynamoDbMaterialRepository.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Materials/Infrastructure/Persistence/DynamoDbMaterialRepository.cs#L137-L188)

The method accepts a `limit` and `cursor` for pagination of the underlying DynamoDB query, but the actual returned collection is a `HashSet<string>` of unique component names *extracted from that page only*. The cursor moves through raw material records, not through unique components. This means:
- Page 1 may return 3 unique components from 10 records
- Page 2 may return overlapping components from the next 10 records

The uniqueness contract is corrupted at the API boundary. Either load all pages server-side (no external pagination) or redesign using a dedicated GSI on component name.

---

### M-6 — [CalculateAllCostsAsync](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/API/Endpoints/CostingEndpoints.cs#181-250) uses `materials.Any()` which enumerates twice

**Rule: §3.3 Performance**

[CostingEndpoints.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/API/Endpoints/CostingEndpoints.cs#L191-L204)

```csharp
IEnumerable<MaterialFormulation> materials = await materialsClient.GetAllMaterialsAsync();
if (!materials.Any())  // first enumeration
    ...
var uniqueComponents = materials.SelectMany(...) // second enumeration
```

[GetAllMaterialsAsync](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Materials/API/Endpoints/MaterialsEndpoints.cs#91-115) returns `List<T>` at runtime, but the declared type is `IEnumerable<T>`. Use a concrete type (`IReadOnlyList<T>`) to document intent and avoid subtle double-enumeration bugs if the implementation were ever changed to be lazy.

---

## 🟡 Minor Issues

### N-1 — Inconsistent `WriteIndented` JSON config between services

`PoC.Materials` sets `WriteIndented = true` in `ConfigureHttpJsonOptions`. `PoC.Costing` and `PoC.Populator` do not. API responses should look consistent across services.

---

### N-2 — Duplicate double-slash fix middleware across all [Program.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Costing/Program.cs) files

The same anonymous middleware for fixing `//` paths is copy-pasted into `PoC.Materials`, `PoC.Costing`, and `PoC.Populator`. This violates DRY and should be extracted into a named extension method in `PoC.Observability` or `PoC.Shared`:

```csharp
public static IApplicationBuilder UseDoubleSlashPathFix(this IApplicationBuilder app) { ... }
```

---

### N-3 — `Result` and `Result<T>` are `class`, not `record`

**Rule: §5.2 Use `record` types for immutable Value Objects**

`Result` and `Error` carry value semantics but `Result` is a `class`. While `Error` is correctly a `record`, `Result<T>` should also be a `sealed record` for structural equality and consistent handling.

---

### N-4 — `LogMaterialIngested` logger method defined but never called in `MaterialIngestionFunction`

[MaterialIngestionFunction.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Materials/Functions/MaterialIngestionFunction.cs#L173-L174)

`LogMaterialIngested` is declared with `[LoggerMessage]` but `LogSuccessfullyIngested` is used instead. Dead logging code should be removed.

---

### N-5 — Architecture Tests do not cover `PoC.FeatureFlags` or `PoC.Observability` libraries

**Rule: §10 Architecture Tests**

[ArchitectureTests.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.ArchitectureTests/ArchitectureTests.cs) only validates that the Shared Kernel doesn't depend on business domains, but it doesn't assert that `PoC.FeatureFlags` or `PoC.Observability` don't accidentally pull in business-domain types. Add rules for these shared libraries.

---

### N-6 — Portuguese comments remain in production code

**Rule: §2 "English is the sole official language"**

In `PoC.Populator/Program.cs` the dead comments contain Portuguese text (`// Lê a versão injetada no build`, `// Imprime no log da AWS/LocalStack`). Must be removed or translated.

---

### N-7 — `OtlpProtocol` comparison uses `.ToLower()` instead of `StringComparison`

[ObservabilityExtensions.cs](file:///d:/Projetos/poc_feature/src/PoC.Observability/Extensions/ObservabilityExtensions.cs#L175)

```diff
- if (options.OtlpProtocol?.ToLower() == "http/protobuf")
+ if (string.Equals(options.OtlpProtocol, "http/protobuf", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
```

`.ToLower()` allocates a new string; `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase` does not.

